ial murder of  gabby petito so  i kind of think that or i thought that  his parents had helped him and that had  he escaped but now that we have found  his body and that it was suicide clearly  he uh you know decided to take that  route  interesting yep we have all the facts  there and that's the seems to be the end  of the gabby potato and brian laundry  saga thank you both coming up on law and  crime daily kyle rinhaus sits down for  his first interview just days after his  acquittal in the kenosha shootings plus  fallout from the deadly waukesha holiday  parade crash why wisconsin officials say  the driver's bond was inappropriately  low  [Music]  welcome back to law and crime daily the  milwaukee county district attorney says  bail was inappropriately low for the man  officials say rammed his suv into a  holiday parade in waukesha wisconsin 39  year old daryl brooks faces five counts  of first-degree intentional homicide  after crashing his vehicle into the  parade on sunday five people were killed  and more than 40 others injured  at the time brooks was driving away from  a domestic disturbance incident all this  comes just five days after brooks was  released from the waukesha county jail  with no charges this comes after he  posted a one thousand dollar bail  several weeks prior in a case where  officials say he ran over the mother of  his child at a gas station before that  he was accused of shooting his nephew in  july of 2020 but scheduling conflicts  preventing his right to a speedy trial  his bail is reduced to 500 in that case  the milwaukee county district attorney's  office says an internal review is now  being conducted on the decision to lower  bail to a thousand dollars  back to break down this tragedy's  retired swat officer and detective lisa  lockwood and terry austin lisa brooks  being released on low bail the charges  he was facing has created an argument  that the prosecution failed in reducing  the bail could these deaths have been  avoided 